{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/858571-2ed-alternate-origins-for-geister","id":858571,"title":"[2ED] Alternate Origins For Geister?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T15:43:14-07:00","id":858571,"title":"[2ED] Alternate Origins For Geister?","content":"From my understanding, Geister are usually considered as ghosts who gradually replaced their Anchors to the living world with aspects of Death. This allows them to acquire Rank 4+ and use their Influences to open Avernian Gates. Therefore, they have greater mobility than the typical ghosts of Rank 1 and 2. The transformation into a minor god of Death likely involves the abandonment of Integrity and the development of new Aspirations related to ghostly phenomena.<br /> <br /> However, some Geister are stranger than others. Sometimes, this can be explained by the Geist in question having died a long time ago and/or eagerly embracing the Underworld. At other times, this explanation is not enough. There are Geister who appear as angelic, demonic or extraterrestrial beings. What if this isn't just a subconscious preference on part of once-human entities? 1ED suggested that the Cthonians might be ghosts or ghostly shreds of non-humans, perhaps including Supernal entities of Stygia who faded away by spending too much time on the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Could the origin of a Geist influence the template of a Sin-Eater beyond giving unique Keys, Ceremonies, ways to regain Plasm and such? Could there be a sixth Threshold for bizarre and/or abstract deaths? If that Threshold exists, is it considered &quot;official&quot; by the Kerberoi and other denizens of the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:33:34-07:00","id":858597,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if a threshold existed for characters killed in esoteric ways, such as a character being killed because they broke a fey bargin and the wyrd gets them, and the geists of the threshold are bound in the laws of the wyrd rather than the laws of the underworld. More Ghost + Gentry than Ghost + Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:40:24-07:00","id":863579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/858571-2ed-alternate-origins-for-geister#post858571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could there be a sixth Threshold for bizarre and/or abstract deaths? If that Threshold exists, is it considered &quot;official&quot; by the Kerberoi and other denizens of the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did come up with a Blessed Threshold (chosen of the Shining Horseman) for people who died in ways that fulfilled a cause that mattered to them. It was little known among Sineaters, because of course people who die in circumstances like that almost never leave ghosts behind. However, they <i>can</i> leave charms and memorabilia behind, and are perhaps even more likely to. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}